The audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants preparing for the West Virginia Class E knowledge examination, reading at a plain-English level with no prior driving knowledge assumed. Section Thirteen teaches how accessible parking and accommodations work and how to enter, travel and leave an interstate safely. It depends on the definitions chapter for interchange, acceleration lane and deceleration lane and on the traffic signs chapter for guide signs and route markers. The rules progress from accessible parking and accommodations, through route numbering and planning, to entering, exiting and traveling on interstates.
